From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:11:16 +0000
Subject: feat(render-android): render small static rotations through the
 canvas matrix

View.rotation is a RenderNode transform, so text rotated by a few degrees
is rasterized unrotated and then resampled by the GPU, which blurs small
glyphs and leaves edges aliased. For static pure-Z rotations up to 15
degrees (no scale/translate, not animation-driven), apply the rotation
through the view decoration canvas matrix instead, alongside skew.
Animation frames keep using View.rotation.

Fork-Patch: render-android-static-rotation-canvas-matrix
Origin: dd76e654
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>

